# Generated training set.
#
# Deliberately not committed. It is rebuilt deterministically from the hobli
# tables by `python -m ml.train --regenerate` (or automatically on first train,
# since ml.train generates it when missing). Committing it would mean a fresh
# clone running `python -m ml.train` silently reuses a dataset built from
# whatever data/ looked like at commit time, which is exactly the staleness trap
# the README warns about.
ml/data/training_data.csv

# The trained model, its metrics and the exported tree rules ARE committed, so
# the app and the /api/model endpoint work on a fresh clone without waiting out
# a 15-minute hyperparameter search.

